<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Mac rule in Cao Bang</h1><p class="st-meta">1593 CE – 1677 CE · capital Cao Bang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A rump Mac state in the northern mountains of Vietnam that survived for eighty years after the Mac lost Thang Long, under Ming and Qing protection.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinh-tung">Trinh Tung</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a> in 1592 and executed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-mau-hop">Mac Mau Hop</a>, members of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mac-dynasty">Mac dynasty</a> fled to the mountainous province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-bang">Cao Bang</a> near the Chinese border. In 1593 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-kinh-cung">Mac Kinh Cung</a> proclaimed himself emperor, and the Ming court pressured the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/later-le-dynasty">Later Le dynasty</a> to leave them in possession.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Mac ruled a small upland territory of Tay and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nung-people">Nung</a> peoples from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-bang">Cao Bang</a>, relying on diplomatic protection from the Ming and then the Qing. They occasionally raided the lowlands, and in 1623, during a Trinh succession crisis, briefly threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Mac supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-three-feudatories">Revolt of the Three Feudatories</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, the Qing withdrew protection, and in 1677 Trinh forces conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-bang">Cao Bang</a>. The last Mac ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-kinh-vu">Mac Kinh Vu</a>, fled to China, ending the dynasty.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1593 CE – 1677 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><cir